# Finding a shared property value
#
# Alice and Bob are both human. A backward N3 rule calls two subjects
# similar when they share a predicate and object, so a forward rule that asks
# whether Alice is similar to Bob concludes :test :is true. It shows a
# backward rule with a variable predicate, used only when asked.

@prefix : <https://eyereasoner.github.io/ns#> .
@prefix log: <http://www.w3.org/2000/10/swap/log#> .

# Two facts with the same predicate and object.
:Alice a :Human .
:Bob a :Human .

# The test: if Alice is similar to Bob, record that the test passed.
{
    :Alice :similar :Bob .
} => {
    :test :is true .
} .

# A is similar to B when some statement about A, with the same predicate and
# object, is also true of B.
{
    ?A :similar ?B .
} <= {
    ?A ?Pred ?Obj .
    ?B ?Pred ?Obj .
} .
